+/**
+ * Runs her outings: one at a time, in the long-lived service, each a loop of
+ * observe → step call → parse → carry out the verb, until she is done or a rule ends it.
+ *
+ * - She starts one with a `go:` line in a moment of hers; the loop hands it here ([go])
+ *   and waits for nothing. It does not start while the service is not running ([start]
+ *   has not been called: "her space is not awake"), while another runs, while she sleeps,
+ *   with fewer than [OwnLedger.Start.OUTING] calls on her own left, or on a low battery or a
+ *   hot phone. Each of those is logged as not started and she is told at her next moment.
+ * - Before every step the rules of [OutingRules] are asked: switched off, asleep (I9),
+ *   three guard refusals, power, and fewer than [OwnLedger.Start.STEP] calls left (I10) end
+ *   it; his talk pauses it, and it goes on [OutingRules.RESUME_AFTER_QUIET_MILLIS] after the
+ *   talk went quiet, or ends after [OutingRules.END_AFTER_PAUSED_MILLIS] paused. Its
+ *   minutes (pauses not counted) and its steps are capped by his settings.
+ * - A step is one call of hers ([Mind.step]); her verbs are carried out by code
+ *   ([ReadingSpace]). Where her eyes are open when it starts ([Eyes]), she may have up to
+ *   [LLMConfig.personaEyesPerOuting] pictures in front of her described (`look <n>`), each
+ *   one call of hers ([OwnPurpose.EYES]) counted in the outing's calls. Her one `say:` of
+ *   the outing goes to him through [Room]; nothing else from an outing reaches his chat,
+ *   and a `>>` in a step is counted and never run (I1).
+ * - It is logged ([HerLog]) with counts, titles and her search words, never what she
+ *   thought, noted or felt (I8); [HerNow] says what she is doing for the notification. A
+ *   RUNNING entry left by an app that was stopped is closed when the service starts again.
+ * - When it ends, she comes back ([Mind.cameBack]): her next moment is brought forward and
+ *   told what she did.
+ * - A `go: look` is a look through the phone's camera ([Looks]), from her own moments only:
+ *   never from a step, whose verbs have no camera. It starts only where [CameraLook.refusal]
+ *   lets it (his screen on and unlocked, no call, no talk of his, the battery, the calls, the
+ *   day's looks, no other app on a camera) and the fold of the phone has a camera facing that
+ *   way. His talk, Stop, his screen going off and a call call it off while it runs (§1.1). Each
+ *   frame stays in memory and goes to her eyes only; he is told each time she looks where his
+ *   settings say so ([Room.looked]). What the describer wrote is shown to her at once in a
+ *   moment of looking (one step of hers, [OutingPrompt.lookText]), a frame with a kid in it as
+ *   kid only. The log gets the camera, the time and counts, never a description (I8).
+ *
+ * Nothing here reaches his phone: no plan, no action, no screen of his, no microphone.
+ */
+@Singleton
+class OutingHost internal constructor(
+    private val mind: Mind,
+    private val sources: ReadingSpace.Sources,
+    private val his: suspend () -> OutgoingGuard.His,
+    private val ledger: OwnLedger,
+    private val log: HerLog,
+    private val herNow: HerNow,
+    private val life: OwnLife,
+    private val headlines: suspend (List<Feeds.Feed>, Long) -> Glance.Look,
+    private val herFeeds: (LLMConfig) -> List<Feeds.Feed>,
+    private val phone: Phone,
+    private val clock: () -> Long,
+    private val wait: suspend (Long) -> Unit,
+    private val scope: CoroutineScope,
+    /** How a go: that asks him first waits out [ASK_WAITS_MILLIS]; the same wait as the rest, unless a test holds it. */
+    private val askWait: suspend (Long) -> Unit = wait,
+    /** Her eyes, for pictures in what she reads; null where she has none. Never a camera. */
+    private val eyes: Eyes? = null,
+    /** Her camera looks, for a `go: look` from a moment of hers; null where she has none. Never handed to a step. */
+    private val looks: Looks? = null,
+    /** His clock at a time, as her moment of looking says it ("14:02"). */
