+ * with the notebook he does on the card screen: hand her notes, copy it out to move her
+ * to another phone, and empty it ([empty]).
+ *
+ * Beside the notes it holds, under the same prefix, what the app has to know between
+ * two runs: the time of her last notebook pass, the unread rows of chats that were
+ * deleted before a pass read them, the lines of a pass that could not be taken and
+ * that she has not been shown yet, the state of her own time, how she feels, the
+ * marks of how she knows a thing, which starting notes the notebook was given and
+ * whether he emptied it. None of these rows is a note of hers: [notes] and
+ * every count of notes leave them out, and they are listed on no screen and copied out
+ * with nothing.
+ *
+ * Nor is her archive: the text a note had before she wrote over it, and every note she
+ * let go or the notebook had no room for. The app never deletes a note of hers on its
+ * own: what leaves her page goes there first ([apply], [fade], [prune]), off her page
+ * and out of her prompts but for the few notes she let go that her sleep pass lists
+ * ([archivedLately]), and a note she let go she can bring back in her sleep ([restore]).
+ * Only the owner's own act of emptying her notebook deletes it ([empty]).
