+     * Consonants English often writes doubled at the end of a word, so a stretched run of
+     * one is cut to two: "allll" is "all", not "al". A voice says "hott" as it says
+     * "hot", so two is the safe side for these.
+     */
+    private const val DOUBLED_CONSONANTS = "lsft"
+
+    /** The vowels English writes both single and doubled, with another sound each time. */
+    private const val DOUBLED_VOWELS = "oe"
+
+    /**
